# Line-ending policy.
#
# All text is stored with LF and checked out with LF, on every platform.
# Prettier writes LF by default (endOfLine: "lf") and its --check compares
# against LF, so a Windows checkout that used CRLF would fail
# `pnpm format:check` locally while passing in Linux CI. Pinning both sides
# to LF keeps local and CI results identical and stops Git's
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings on every diff.
#
# This is a normalisation rule, not a rewrite: Git applies it to files it
# reads from here on, so no existing file is mass-converted.
* text=auto eol=lf
